<FONT SIZE="1" color="#a62a2a" face="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
posted August 10, 2001 10:20 AM &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_profile&u=00000002" target=_blank>
<IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/profile_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Profile for Verser"></A>  &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000002"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/priv_message.gif" BORDER='0' ALT="Send New Private Message"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=edit_post&f=1&t=000086&reply_num=000001&u=00000002"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/edit_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Edit/Delete Post"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=reply&f=1&t=000086&replyto=000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/quote_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Reply With Quote"></A>
</FONT>
<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
1) PoGs are a pain in the ass.  VI has fixed them to where PoG supression doesn't work anymore.  Not that I intended to do that, but it would've been nice to keep a few cyles supressed while we got our heads screwed on right.  Also...if you become visible, you are on the PoG's hate list..so going inviso again...does nothing.  They are still coming after you.<P>2) Tranquil Treants are death incarnate.  We just could not stop it from gating.<P>3) Pathing has been changed a little in there.  <BR>3a) All mobs now path closer to the wall.<BR>3b) A treant paths around the entire zone up on the wall.<P>4) Need..and I mean need at least 1 55+ enchanter that can get interrupts off.  Preferrably more.  I;m really not sure if these things can be stunned though. So maybe knockback type spells need to be used.  Like, 2-3 mages chain casting their 2 second casting 8th lvl Shock of Swords, Clerics casting their 29th lvl stun, and anything else that have knockback.<P>5) I need someone to take charge of the battle.  Me dieing right away or kiting adds while twisting 2 songs just does not give me anytime to say more then, "Yes", "N11o"...etc...  <P>Or...I just need to let someone else pull while I keep a closer eye on what's happening.<P>6) Need more clerics.<P>7) Need more 54+ tanks types that can hold aggro.<P>8 )  I would say we need people to listen better too, but I feel responsible for that, and due to #5, I just can't blame anyone else for not knowing what to do in tight situations.  We needed a clear voice in all of the chaos last night and I just couldn't provide that.  <P>9) The Loot...we had some warrior legs drop off the first thing we killed, but due to also dealing with 2 PoGs and the Whirl of Energy and maybe some more adds after I died and maybe a total wipe out...I just didn't see how we could've got all the warriors that died rezzed back in time to have a their deserved shot at winning them.  I also wasn't sure how long the corpse would last before poofing.  So, that is why, during my naked run from SS,  I told Svenalo to just have the remaining warriors roll.  <P>10) Camp Site.  Our old "safe spot" really isn't safe as it used to be.   The Red Sky raid that followed went to the <B>  SouthWest corner</B>...high up in the corner.  I didn't see any wanderers path near enough to aggro there.  The Treant did come by, but that was after we had killed a few things and started to move to the next "camp".  So it probably just pathed close and aggro'ed.  However; they managed to keep it from gating.<P>11) KOS/Non-KOS...having a non-KOS 49+ cleric and porter..that's a good thing.  The cleric can rezz folks without causing aggro to themselves.  Saves the clerics fighting some mana and definitly helps for CR.<P>12) I have no idea if I ever want to try and lead a raid again.  I <B>  hate</B> losing to things that I feel like the team assembled can beat.  I hate having tons of people dead and nasty CR issues.  I guess everyone hates that too, but it's even worse when it's "your" raid.   <IMG SRC="frown.gif" border="0">  <P>13) If inviso drops during zone in...just run a little east and let the Whirl of Energy kill you before the PoG's come.<P>14) Thanks to everyone that did come though.  Congrats to Dergoth on his Warrior legs.  I really wish we could have got the people that bled for no reason get more payback.  I'll probably forget how painful this one was in a month or so and try again...but g-damn...I wonder if anyone would be stupid enough to sign up?  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song<BR>Sleethr - 54th DE Mage<BR>Medec - 41st level Battle Cleric<BR>Meekka - 31st DE Rogue<BR>Vowk - 27th Dr00d
</FONT>
